<title>USA: Santa Fe Energy sets defensive rights.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe Energy sets defensive rights.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Fe Energy Resources said on Wednesday that its board of directors has adopted a shareholder rights plan with a 15 percent trigger.</p>
<p>Under the plan, preferred stock purchase rights will be distributed to holders of the company's common stock and would be exercisable if a party acquired beneficial ownership of 15 percent or more of Santa Fe Energy's common stock, or began a tender offer which would result in ownership of 15 percent or more of such stock.</p>
<p>The company said it is not aware of any effort to acquire control of it.</p>
</text>
